=== Entry gate: the factorisation contract ===

At r = 0 with diagonal Phi, Theta and Sigma the likelihood factorises,
so the joint fit must equal the sum of the univariate fits exactly.

  univariate 1 (p=2, q=0)   logL =     -27.1020487851
  univariate 2 (p=2, q=0)   logL =     -20.3366447449
                                 sum  =     -47.4386935301
                                 joint=     -47.4386935301
  (both sides untruncated; the fit's own logL, xi truncated at 1e-03, is -47.4386935301)

  crossing identity (joint - sum) = -5.009e-12   (tolerance 1.0e-06)   VERIFIED
  rung 1  (F diag, Theta diag, Sigma free)   logL = -43.8036850507
  rung 2  (F free, Theta free, Sigma free)   logL = -29.4941825830

